    "text": "The bar chart compares the proportions of households separating household waste in North and South in 2010, 2015 and 2020. All figures are expressed as percentages.\n\nOverall, the proportion in North increased overall, whereas South increased overall. North recorded the higher figure at the end of the period. The difference between the regions was unchanged, from 15 percentage points in 2010 to 15 points in 2020.\n\nIn North, the figure stood at 24% in 2010, before rising to 49% five years later. It then increased to 74% in 2020. The first interval saw a change of 25 percentage points, while the corresponding movement during the second half of the decade was 25 points.\n\nSouth followed a different pattern, starting at 39% and reaching 54% in 2015. By 2020, its figure was 59%. Comparing the two regions directly, South had the larger share at the beginning, while North led at the end. The final figures of 74% for North and 59% for South therefore show a gap of 15 percentage points.",
